exercises.problem:
For each of the following pairs, indicate which one of the two species is larger:
(a) <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><msup><mi>&#x0004E;</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math> or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><msup><mi>&#x00046;</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math>;
(b) <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math> or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math>;
(c) <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math> or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math>

Predict which element of the following pairs will have the higher density and support your prediction using periodic trends :
(a) Cr or W ;
(b) W or Os;
(c) Pd or Ag ; and
(d) Y or Nb .

